    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 74,
        "text": "Hi, I'm Maya from the city transport office. Thanks for coming, Leo.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "5d4af666600cf6948bfaef22a24855747b593923c6db8aec3049757fe46a3145",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 80,
        "sourceEnd": 181,
        "text": "No problem. I read your email about the bike-share data. You want me to look at the prediction model?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "feeb228c227631243b89c78ae3832e73c0c2440b934c5d52618335c921a144ed",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 188,
        "sourceEnd": 346,
        "text": "Yes. Last month we used a model to predict how many bikes people would take from each station. It worked well on weekdays, but on weekends it was often wrong.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "27f8898bdf13aee452390a6de05bf49288a9ebb811b465db5d69e9f5cb4580ef",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 352,
        "sourceEnd": 383,
        "text": "How wrong? Do you have numbers?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "4c4d3000c741db7609e0f84c320f5a5a91e865c8ce05bb7631e03ecaac0cf057",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 390,
        "sourceEnd": 563,
        "text": "On a normal Tuesday, the model predicted 420 rides, and the real number was 415. That's very close. But on a sunny Saturday, it predicted 300 rides, and we actually had 610.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "b0bcf94622565f14916a45740ed9d1a0a83fe000667b2bede01316ba54003c4b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 569,
        "sourceEnd": 640,
        "text": "So the model missed the weekend leisure trips. Did it use weather data?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "14c5067812c274713db01cc476188d13440d904d6203ed1e4db51e2ebf5b7172",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 647,
        "sourceEnd": 764,
        "text": "It used temperature and rain, but not sunshine hours or school holidays. Also, it only looked at the past six months.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "626202cf06e8282d68a044b2c787335e072b6b2df628ed186544bdba116f12a0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 770,
        "sourceEnd": 907,
        "text": "Six months is short. You need at least two years to see seasonal patterns. And the model probably learned mostly from commuter behaviour.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "35aa0fc03a2bb678a24574af9245395d96b6a0ab737df6877e301d9e7b6406ff",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 914,
        "sourceEnd": 1059,
        "text": "That's what I thought. The model is good at regular patterns, but it fails when people change their habits, like on holidays or during festivals.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "6a050849f6e95d04b7bd9d281220693cb997f5c4d408bd6996836f18088ffd14",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1065,
        "sourceEnd": 1209,
        "text": "Right. A prediction model is not a magic ball. It finds patterns in old data. If the future is different from the past, the model will be wrong.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "1349f80537e5c1becfabf00eb68b7cb2cba43a3a2af776abe3b1bcf652c96059",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1216,
        "sourceEnd": 1281,
        "text": "So what should we do? We can't collect two years of data quickly.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "af800a7700441490159c34c5878918e84269d94e1f39f153aa78ad39c446b2d5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1287,
        "sourceEnd": 1449,
        "text": "You can add simple rules. For example, if the forecast says sunny and over 25 degrees, add 30 percent more bikes to popular parks. And check the model every week.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "ff067aedad91a87b2ee0a4515ec9b130302e2d9928b0372338b71364f9cffc2d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1456,
        "sourceEnd": 1540,
        "text": "That sounds practical. But our manager wants one perfect model that works every day.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "8d03fbc339287e5d02e53bbe4785fb9e321d9151865503af14bcec4f83793d5d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1546,
        "sourceEnd": 1679,
        "text": "No model is perfect. Even the best model has limits. The important thing is to know when to trust it and when to use human judgement.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "a0e039c9f1a077867a577aaeed4cf84243f54fd464eaec61bcfc00599738095e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1686,
        "sourceEnd": 1753,
        "text": "OK. Can you write a short report for our manager? Maybe five pages?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "993af3182497bf1610936d778f7382e7224002676d660edce7d29c68a7d2d324",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1759,
        "sourceEnd": 1872,
        "text": "Five pages is fine. I'll include the weekday success and the weekend failure. I'll also suggest the simple rules.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "3b24427e12225dd577eadca148aeb1a98d4cd837fb0da4e8d7f33578ca75e57b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1879,
        "sourceEnd": 2035,
        "text": "Great. One more thing: the model predicted 50 bikes for a small station near the university, but we found only 12 bikes there. The station was almost empty.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "0a57f55a97209e27c106dcf5314a02f339d3509da0114b3f17e229aae237abcb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2041,
        "sourceEnd": 2196,
        "text": "That's a supply problem, not a prediction problem. If there are no bikes, people can't take them. The model should also check how many bikes are available.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "cce12a3c9e0b8ad8b8647b15d0f9b4c5561e77636f80857282b717d164730b64",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2203,
        "sourceEnd": 2290,
        "text": "Good point. I'll add that to the report. So the model needs bike availability data too.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "6c9f9d2acdfe5b98b7dde1562b420632c069a1d737cbd147e64e02a704622363",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2296,
        "sourceEnd": 2377,
        "text": "Exactly. And remember: a model is a tool, not a boss. People still need to think.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "a3054bd6de4b9adb219697c3b41f62a11224dd7bb02151aacfcac3b81098361d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2384,
        "sourceEnd": 2432,
        "text": "Thanks, Leo. I'll send you the data files today.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "e4f1a4bf83a9ee21067c8ab69a5de0572e59e845bf72713442b566609165ead4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2438,
        "sourceEnd": 2475,
        "text": "Perfect. I'll start tomorrow morning.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "83f8079c6e574c06b909b4e27744e35a264f4490c8ad49e8e8679d81d0dee126",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 2477,
        "sourceEnd": 2496,
        "text": "[Expanded section:]",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-BrianNeural",
        "textHash": "c2d193eae617a1228c5b51c3dd7a2b6422d89b651b2d95c4f948d32ecd5afbd8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2503,
        "sourceEnd": 2640,
        "text": "Before we finish, I want to make sure I understand the bigger picture. Why do you think the model failed so badly on that sunny Saturday?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "758ba8a02642646d3f53223ddc7c86b927a91783d9ac3e4bd2b5c0e877352df5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2646,
        "sourceEnd": 2949,
        "text": "There are a few reasons. First, the model was trained mostly on weekday commuter trips, where people use bikes to get to work or school at regular times. On weekends, people ride for leisure, and their behaviour depends on things like sunshine, events, and holidays. The model didn't have those signals.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "3f1c7565a1cad7a3ffeff727e58360407b6953fbefffdae07fadff5f8960aff0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2956,
        "sourceEnd": 2996,
        "text": "So it's not just about adding more data?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "1050f41c699b8c2a5c6c36913077d6e63a5f41e20a28276e8ec9125e68efa4a3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 3002,
        "sourceEnd": 3261,
        "text": "More data helps, but you also need the right data. If you collect two years of data but still ignore sunshine hours and school holidays, the model will still miss weekend peaks. You need to include those variables and maybe use a different model for weekends.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "59357bf3fbfebaa6c2b7e1200a8bab0ab7a4b05ee97c4ceabfbf2f0e29dd3af5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3268,
        "sourceEnd": 3368,
        "text": "That makes sense. What about the small station near the university? Could that also be a data issue?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "f8f8561e5b5d085336f44837161908ac841f7159d79468f1df9abcdc05a5e1ce",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 3374,
        "sourceEnd": 3595,
        "text": "Partly. The model predicted 50 bikes, but only 12 were available. That's a supply problem. The model should check real-time bike availability before making predictions. Otherwise, it's predicting demand that can't be met.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "b05c5a54dedf174da2a857d36676e87b08dda087340f754299291e9e482fcb78",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3602,
        "sourceEnd": 3655,
        "text": "So we need to combine prediction with real-time data.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ec8194193777519df352c903db7a38821cdadfe04346f0f5631dbf52d6eef9fc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 3661,
        "sourceEnd": 3817,
        "text": "Exactly. And that's why human judgement is still important. A model can tell you what might happen, but a person needs to check if the conditions are right.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2ebee82841a94a79ada3b7cd166f10edbe37e0c1e767992803620c1b628236a7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3824,
        "sourceEnd": 3893,
        "text": "I'll make sure the report covers these points. Thanks for explaining.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "5fdd52f207ab3df55b46f9be8ac557d30c90a09a3e4fe27263880296f8020725",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 3899,
        "sourceEnd": 3955,
        "text": "You're welcome. I'll get started on the report tomorrow.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "1f17c190dee000b4431e2a0735bc951b18f8b449a0207441111a782883d3b484",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
